## Connected behavior

The engine now persists human_gm / ai_dm mode and a changing authority epoch. A paused, human-owned handoff delegates a restricted AI principal while retaining the human GM identity. Old authority cannot make new changes. Recorded commands can still recover their original receipts after a handoff or restart.

The real createCampaignAI path now schedules a delegated narrative director in AI mode. It handles pending describe, talk, and interact intentions through the existing gm_resolve engine command. It does not implement arbitrary mechanical rulings, full NPC planning, or the entire AI-DM design. Existing AI player companions and human approval of generated scene art remain in place.

EngineClient now preserves an explicitly supplied authorityEpoch while retaining the original shape of legacy requests. The director captures its principal, epoch, and revision; validates authority around inference; sends only selected scene/intention context; and recovers the original receipt after an ambiguous network outcome without issuing a second command.

## Private-service contract

The on-disk Obus game service accepts scope.role host, not gm, for this request. The adapter uses task intent with local-only, nonexportable routing and Codex disabled. Inline evidence omits top-level contract and question: contract would trigger signed-reference validation, and question would enable automatic retrieval. The adapter must whitelist evidence because inline content is serialized into the model prompt.

The private game endpoint defaults to loopback port 38175. This machine's recovery documentation identifies port 38178. A current listener check found neither port listening, and the default authenticated capability request failed to connect. The general Obus dashboard remains a separate service and must not substitute for the private game route.

No live model inference, Discord campaign mutation, or private-service restart has been performed in this continuation. A supported clean-start path is being investigated. Live runtime lease, session policy, and route validation remain necessary before an end-to-end test.

